## Context

Phase 1 of 0270's migration path: `dyne` alone -- format plus
`open/show/list/check`; the forge stays the authority. One codebase,
two specs: dyne shares erg's parser, atomic-write and validator
machinery as internal modules; argv[0] picks the personality of one
busybox-style blob.

## Scope

- argv[0] dispatch in the shared binary; identical blob committed at
  `tickets/erg` and `tickets/merges/dyne` (one content-addressed blob, two
  checkout paths); the size ratchet covers it
- `dyne open`: create `tickets/merges/<branch>.dyne` for the current branch
  (Source = branch, Target defaulting to main), refuse an existing one
- `dyne show`: render the file, log entries reordered by timestamp
- `dyne list`: an MR is open iff Source is not an ancestor of Target
  (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`); enumeration is as fresh as the
  last fetch -- document, per 0270's hard points
- `dyne check`: corpus checks over `tickets/merges/` -- duplicate headers are
  a hard error (the union-merge fence), malformed files, magic/version
- invariants hold: offline (shells out to git, no network code),
  standalone (static binary, POSIX, zero third-party deps), stateless,
  fast, small; infrastructure-class posture from day one (reproducible
  offline build, signed tags)

## Testing

House policy: Go unit tests own pure-function correctness (parsing,
DAG-state predicate); shell integration tests own CLI black-box
behavior.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] dogfood: this repo carries `tickets/merges/` with the committed dyne blob
- [ ] the four commands behave per the %dyne 0.1 spec; make test green

## Author design amendment (2026-10-15)

Read `docs/dyne-review-contract.md` as the current amendment to 0270.
It supersedes the earlier root merges/ placement: use tickets/merges/,
with evidence under tickets/reviews/. Keep the Go/static/shared-codebase
plan and independent commands; no new path configuration or erg dependency.
The Dyne body carries the evolving plan; Hunt owns it and gaze executes it.
Preserve immutable per-pass requests/results and revision-bound evidence.
Open reuse, stop, concurrency and recovery questions are recorded for author
discussion, not silently settled. Follow the delivery phases in that document;
this ticket remains open and no implementation is claimed.
